"use strict";

/* generated from story/scenes/act1_ch1.md — do not edit */

SC["a1c1_ferry"]={t:()=>SYS(`CHAPTER ONE — THE GOLD-HAIRED GHOST`)+P(`You will not remember this part.`)+P(`The first person to find you is not a girl with mint on her hands. It is Old Shan the ferryman, poling home through the reed-shallows with the last of the light, who sees a pale shape face-down in the green and stops poling.`)+P(`He looks for a long time. He is not a cruel man. But gold hair means foreign, and foreign means trouble, and drowned means ghost — and a ferryman who hauls a ghost aboard poles it home to his own door. He makes the sign against evil, twice, carefully, and gives you back to the river.`)+P(`The current, which has already carried you between worlds, is not offended. It turns you once, almost gently, and sets you down on the herb-gatherers' bank instead — the one bank on this whole river where, in about four minutes, a girl will be cutting mint.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Wake up properly this time.`,go:"c1_wake"}]};

SC["c1_wake"]={t:()=>P(`You wake coughing river water onto somebody's herb basket. A girl your age crouches over you, sleeves rolled, hands smelling of crushed mint. A round boy hovers behind her with a boat hook held like he expects you to bite.`)+P(`“He's alive,” the girl says. Then she sees your hair and goes very still. “Bao. Look at his hair.”`)+P(`“Gold,” the boy whispers. “Like a ghost. Or a demon. Mei, we should—”`)+P(`“We should get him dry,” Mei says, in the tone of someone who has already decided.`)+P(`The language is nothing you have ever heard, and you understand every word of it. Something in your chest hums when you notice that — a single warm fiber, pulled tight. The Loom did not drop you here unaltered.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`“Thank you. I'm ${G.name}.” Be honest about being lost.`,do:()=>{G.mei++;note("Mei +1");},go:"a1c1_shed"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Say nothing yet. Watch. Learn the shape of this place first.`,do:()=>{addIns(1);},go:"a1c1_shed"}]};

SC["a1c1_shed"]={t:()=>P(`Mei's grandmother is a small woman made of knuckles and silence. She looks at your hair for exactly as long as it takes to decide it isn't her problem, then points her chin at the drying shed and ladles you a bowl of congee you did not ask for and could not have asked for better.`)+P(`The shed smells of forty kinds of cut green. Herb bundles hang from the rafters like quiet bells. Moonlight comes through the wall-slats in stripes, and somewhere below, the river that killed you and carried you keeps saying the same soft thing over and over.`)+((G.f.bg==="sister")?(P(`You think: right now, by some clock in some world, the porch light is on. She'll have left it on. She'll leave it on tomorrow, too. You fold that thought up small and put it where you can't reach it by accident.`)):(((G.f.bg==="music")?(P(`You lie there sorting the night into parts — river under everything, wind section in the rafters, one cricket keeping bad time. Eight bars, no resolution. Story of your life. Both of them.`)):(((G.f.bg==="code")?(P(`You lie there doing what you always do with a system you don't understand: inputs, outputs, constraints. Input: died. Output: here. Constraint: nobody else seems to find flying on swords remarkable. Insufficient data. Sleep on it.`)):(P(`You lie there running the day like a form, beat by beat, looking for where your balance went. There wasn't a mistake to find. Sometimes the throw just comes from outside the mat.`))))))),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Catalogue everything in the shed until your eyes give out. Knowledge is footing.`,do:()=>{addIns(1);},go:"a1c1_rumors"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Let the river talk you down into sleep. Tomorrow needs you whole.`,do:()=>{addStat("heart",1);},go:"a1c1_rumors"}]};

SC["a1c1_rumors"]={t:()=>P(`By the time you carry water up from the well the next morning, the village has already decided what you are — three different ways.`)+P(`By the well, a boatwright's wife swears you are a river god's son, drowned and returned, and that turning you away means floods. Outside the grain-shed, two old men agree you are a demon-child, and that the only question is whether you burn better wet or dry. And trailing you at a careful distance, three small children have concluded, loudly, that you are a foreign prince who has lost his ship, his army, and his shoes.`)+P(`Bao, hauling the other bucket, grins sideways at you. “Pick one,” he says. “Trust me. A story they chose beats a story they're afraid of.”`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Let the river-god story stand. Mystery feeds the kind.`,do:()=>{G.f.a1_rumor="god";addStat("heart",1);note("The village half-bows, half-flinches. Offerings of salt fish appear at the shed door.");},go:"c1_village"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Let them keep the demon story. Fear keeps distance, and distance is information.`,do:()=>{G.f.a1_rumor="demon";addIns(1);note("The well-line goes quiet when you pass. You hear everything they say behind you.");},go:"c1_village"},
  {id:"c2",l:`Be the shipwrecked prince. Bow like you imagine princes bow.`,do:()=>{G.f.a1_rumor="prince";addStat("mind",1);note("Bao appoints himself your royal steward on the spot and cannot stop laughing.");},go:"c1_village"}]};

SC["c1_village"]={t:()=>P(`Cloudrest Village clings to the foot of a mountain that goes up past sense, its peak swallowed by a permanent ring of cloud. Mei points with her chin: “Azure Cloud Sect. In three days the elders descend for the intake trial. Every child of fourteen years may stand the Spirit Tester.” Her voice is careful, hungry. “Even you, river-ghost. Even me.”`)+P(`Bao snorts. “They'll never take a gold-haired foreigner. Or a herb-girl. Or me.” But he says it the way people say things they are praying to be wrong about.`)+P(`Three days. The villagers eye your hair, make signs against evil, and let Mei's grandmother put you up in the drying shed anyway. How do you spend the days?`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Train with Bao — he knows village wrestling, and you remember more than this body should.`,do:()=>{addStat("body",1);G.bao+=2;note("Bao +2");},go:"a1c1_faces"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Help Mei harvest and sort herbs for the trial-day market.`,do:()=>{addStat("heart",1);G.mei+=2;note("Mei +2");},go:"a1c1_faces"},
  {id:"c2",l:`Borrow the village's one battered cultivation primer and read it twice.`,do:()=>{addStat("mind",1);addIns(1);},go:"a1c1_faces"}]};

SC["a1c1_faces"]={t:()=>P(`Trial morning. The whole valley funnels into the village plaza before dawn, and the line of fourteen-year-olds forms up under the eyes of everyone they have ever known.`)+P(`Ahead of you stands a farm girl in a patched festival dress — Hu Lan, the miller's daughter, breathing like she's about to dive into deep water. Behind you, a merchant's son in city silk practices a calm expression that doesn't fit him yet. Bao tells jokes down the line with his palms sweating. Mei doesn't speak at all. She is watching the bronze stand at the head of the plaza the way the hungry watch a kitchen door.`)+P(`You understand the shape of it before anyone explains: this line is the only door in the valley. Everything else is walls.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Watch the orb work. If it can read children, you want to read it.`,do:()=>{addIns(1);},go:"c1_trial"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Watch the families. The orb only tells you about qi.`,do:()=>{addStat("heart",1);},go:"c1_trial"}]};

SC["c1_trial"]={t:()=>P(`Trial day. The elders descend on swords — actually, literally, standing on flying swords, and your Earth-born brain does a small somersault and files it under <i>new physics</i>.`)+P(`The Spirit Tester is a sphere of cloudy jade on a bronze stand. Child after child lays a palm on it. For most it stays dark. For a few it glows: white for spirit roots, blue for water, once a roar of red and a whole family weeping with joy.`)+P(`Hu Lan touches it, and it glows the deep root-red of a banked fire. A clerk strikes her family's name from the grain-debt rolls then and there; her father cries into his hat without a sound. Two children later, the merchant's son gets darkness, total and undramatic, and his father's face closes like a ledger. The boy walks back through the crowd carefully, like something already broken that hasn't been dropped yet.`)+P(`Mei's turn: a faint, steady green. “Herb-spirit root. Outer court,” drones the elder. Bao: dark. He laughs like it doesn't matter.`)+P(`Your turn. The plaza goes quiet — they all want to see what the gold-haired ghost is. You lay your palm on the jade.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`…`,go:"c1_crippled"}]};

SC["c1_crippled"]={t:()=>P(`Nothing. Not dark — <i>wrong</i>. The jade fogs like a window breathed on, then squeals, a hairline crack crawling across its surface. The crowd recoils.`)+P(`“Meridians sealed,” the testing elder pronounces, distaste plain. “Crippled. Worse than empty — the boy is a hole the qi falls into. Next.”`)+P(`But behind him, a tall elder in iron-grey robes has gone motionless, and the stillness on him is the stillness of a man pricing something to the copper. The grey one's name, you will learn, is Elder Kang. He says one word to the steward: “Kitchens.”`)+SYS(`The sect takes you as a SERVANT DISCIPLE. Not a cultivator. A mop with legs. Mei enters the outer court; Bao is hired to haul firewood up the thousand steps.`)+P(`The crowd is already forgetting you — the orb has more children to judge. Only three people in the plaza are still looking at the gold-haired failure: Mei, who looks stricken; Bao, who looks relieved you'll be on the mountain at all; and a thin steward with ink-stained cuffs, who is looking at you the way a man looks at a dropped coin he suspects is foreign currency.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Follow the steward's ledger down the mountain's throat.`,go:"a1c1_qiu"}]};

SC["a1c1_qiu"]={t:()=>P(`Steward Qiu, kitchen-master of the lower terraces, owns a writing brush worn down like an old tooth and a ledger that has never once been closed in front of witnesses. He inspects you the way he'd inspect delivered cabbage.`)+P(`“One boy,” he recites as he writes, “gold-haired. Crippled. Cannot cultivate, cannot carry messages above the third terrace, cannot be seen at festivals.” The brush pauses. “Value: two meals a day. Deductible.”`)+P(`The kitchens of the Azure Cloud Sect are a country of their own — a cellar nation of steam and shouting, of debts written small and grudges written smaller, ruled from a cutting board by a vast woman the whole mountain calls Auntie Tang, who looks up from a cleaver's downstroke exactly once as Qiu leads you through, and watches him — not you — the way cooks watch rats.`)+P(`There are rules down here, and you can feel them like current. Nobody will tell you what they are. Everyone will know when you break one.`)+P(`“Water duty,” Qiu says, closing the ledger on your name. “Dawn and dusk. Break a bucket and it's a week's meals.” He smiles thinly. “Welcome to the mountain, foreign coin.”`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Take up the buckets. The mountain's first evening waits.`,go:"a1c3_trip"}]};

SC["a1c3_trip"]={t:()=>P(`That first evening, as you carry water past the outer court dormitories, a big outer disciple named Liu Feng sticks out his foot. You go down hard. Buckets everywhere. Laughter.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Swallow it. Bow, apologize, mop it up. Watch his stance as you do.`,do:()=>{addIns(1);},go:"a1c2_hierarchy"},
  {id:"c1",l:`“Your foot was in the road. Roads are for walking.” Cold, level, unblinking.`,do:()=>{G.f.mouthy=true;},go:"c1_feng_fight"},
  {id:"c2",l:`He's still laughing. Hit him.`,go:"c1_feng_fight"}]};